ote":null,"reading":"reading:d1059bccc2b4aa34802fb63f","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":"Custom 'amenable': `InvariantMean G` (positive, `toLinearMap 1 = 1`, `toLinearMap (leftPull h f) = toLinearMap f` on ℓ^∞(G, ℝ)) is the standard invariant-mean definition but is not a Mathlib notion; F itself is hand-defined (Group structure is existentially provided inside the theorem).","gap":null,"note":"`thompson_F_nonamenable_composition : ∃ group : Group F, (∀ h g x, (h * g) x = h (g x)) ∧ ¬ Nonempty (InvariantMean F)` where `F := {f : IntervalHomeomorph // StrictMono f ∧ HasDyadicPLPieces f}` (dyadic breakpoints, slopes 2^k via `DyadicPLWitness`) with group law forced to be composition, and `InvariantMean G` = positive normalized left-invariant linear functional on `lp (fun _ : G => ℝ) ∞`. Exactly the nonamenability of Thompson's F.","reading":"reading:ed758a3f31b41a4f5bc4b578","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:d1059bccc2b4aa34802fb63f","reading:ed758a3f31b41a4f5bc4b578"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"755c4b729512c7e2c7d1d3303eb9706f5adf1681","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine","source":"cert-machine","url":"https://carlostoledo.co/reports/openai-math.html"},"id":"reading:d1059bccc2b4aa34802fb63f","pair_review":